inaoftime-scrn-11.png" sizes="(min-width: 1025px) 650px, calc(100vw - 30px)" class="img" type="image/webp" /&gt;             &lt;source srcset="https://npr.brightspotcdn.com/dims3/default/strip/false/crop/3840x2160+0+0/resize/400/quality/85/format/png/?url=http%3A%2F%2Fnpr-brightspot.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fbc%2F68%2Fcae527114c97a9cdea6377147af2%2Fns2-thelegendofzeldaocarinaoftime-scrn-11.png 400w, https://npr.brightspotcdn.com/dims3/default/strip/false/crop/3840x2160+0+0/resize/600/quality/85/format/png/?url=http%3A%2F%2Fnpr-brightspot.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fbc%2F68%2Fcae527114c97a9cdea6377147af2%2Fns2-thelegendofzeldaocarinaoftime-scrn-11.png 600w, https://npr.brightspotcdn.com/dims3/default/strip/false/crop/3840x2160+0+0/resize/800/quality/85/format/png/?url=http%3A%2F%2Fnpr-brightspot.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fbc%2F68%2Fcae527114c97a9cdea6377147af2%2Fns2-thelegendofzeldaocarinaoftime-scrn-11.png 800w, https://npr.brightspotcdn.com/dims3/default/strip/false/crop/3840x2160+0+0/resize/900/quality/85/format/png/?url=http%3A%2F%2Fnpr-brightspot.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fbc%2F68%2Fcae527114c97a9cdea6377147af2%2Fns2-thelegendofzeldaocarinaoftime-scrn-11.png 900w, https://npr.brightspotcdn.com/dims3/default/strip/false/crop/3840x2160+0+0/resize/1200/quality/85/format/png/?url=http%3A%2F%2Fnpr-brightspot.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fbc%2F68%2Fcae527114c97a9cdea6377147af2%2Fns2-thelegendofzeldaocarinaoftime-scrn-11.png 1200w, https://npr.brightspotcdn.com/dims3/default/strip/false/crop/3840x2160+0+0/resize/1600/quality/85/format/png/?url=http%3A%2F%2Fnpr-brightspot.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fbc%2F68%2Fcae527114c97a9cdea6377147af2%2Fns2-thelegendofzeldaocarinaoftime-scrn-11.png 1600w, https://npr.brightspotcdn.com/dims3/default/strip/false/crop/3840x2160+0+0/resize/1800/quality/85/format/png/?url=http%3A%2F%2Fnpr-brightspot.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fbc%2F68%2Fcae527114c97a9cdea6377147af2%2Fns2-thelegendofzeldaocarinaoftime-scrn-11.png 1800w" data-template="https://npr.brightspotcdn.com/dims3/default/strip/false/crop/3840x2160+0+0/resize/{width}/quality/{quality}/format/{format}/?url=http%3A%2F%2Fnpr-brightspot.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fbc%2F68%2Fcae527114c97a9cdea6377147af2%2Fns2-thelegendofzeldaocarinaoftime-scrn-11.png" sizes="(min-width: 1025px) 650px, calc(100vw - 30px)" class="img" type="image/png" /&gt;             &lt;img src="https://npr.brightspotcdn.com/dims3/default/strip/false/crop/3840x2160+0+0/resize/1100/quality/50/format/png/?url=http%3A%2F%2Fnpr-brightspot.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fbc%2F68%2Fcae527114c97a9cdea6377147af2%2Fns2-thelegendofzeldaocarinaoftime-scrn-11.png" data-template="https://npr.brightspotcdn.com/dims3/default/strip/false/crop/3840x2160+0+0/resize/{width}/quality/{quality}/format/{format}/?url=http%3A%2F%2Fnpr-brightspot.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fbc%2F68%2Fcae527114c97a9cdea6377147af2%2Fns2-thelegendofzeldaocarinaoftime-scrn-11.png" class="img" alt="The titular Princess Zelda, reworked for the Nintendo Switch 2 remake of The Legend of Zelda: Ocarina of Time." loading="lazy" /&gt;         &lt;/picture&gt; &lt;/div&gt; &lt;div class="credit-caption"&gt;     &lt;div class="caption-wrap"&gt;         &lt;div class="caption" aria-label="Image caption"&gt;             &lt;p&gt;                 The titular Princess Zelda, reworked for the Nintendo Switch 2 remake of &lt;em&gt;The Legend of Zelda: Ocarina of Time.&lt;/em&gt;                 &lt;b class="credit" aria-label="Image credit"&gt;                                          Nintendo                                      &lt;/b&gt;                 &lt;b class="hide-caption"&gt;&lt;b&gt;&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/b&gt;             &lt;/p&gt;         &lt;/div&gt;               &lt;button class="toggle-caption" aria-label=""&gt;               &lt;svg class="icon icon--info"&gt;&lt;use href="#icon-info"&gt;&lt;/use&gt;&lt;/svg&gt;               &lt;b&gt;&lt;/b&gt;                 &lt;abbr title="Toggle Caption" class="toggle-caption__info"&gt;i&lt;/abbr&gt;              &lt;/button&gt;     &lt;/div&gt;       &lt;/div&gt;    &lt;/div&gt;    &lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Check out what &lt;/strong&gt;&lt;a href="https://www.npr.org/sections/culture/" target="_blank"&gt;&lt;strong&gt;NPR&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/a&gt;&lt;strong&gt; is watching, reading and listening to this weekend:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;   &lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;🍿 Movies: &lt;/strong&gt;&lt;em&gt;Other Mommy&lt;/em&gt;, starring Jessica Chastain, follows a 7-year-old who is visited by a mysterious entity that takes the form of her mother. &lt;em&gt;Pop Culture Happy Hour&lt;/em&gt; describes it as an intense horror film &lt;a href="https://www.npr.org/2026/10/14/nx-s1-6000113/should-we-be-sleeping-on-other-mommy" target="_blank"&gt;filled with dark family secrets&lt;/a&gt;.&lt;/p&gt;       &lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;📺 TV: &lt;/strong&gt;&lt;a href="https://www.npr.org/2026/10/15/nx-s1-6001536/were-high-up-on-the-lowdown" target="_blank"&gt;&lt;em&gt;The Lowdown&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/a&gt; is back for its second season, featuring Ethan Hawke as a freelance investigative reporter entangled with a prominent Tulsa family.&lt;/p&gt;   &lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;📚 Books: &lt;/strong&gt;&lt;a href="https://www.npr.org/2026/10/14/nx-s1-5996628/two-saddest-kitchens-review-roz-chast-jason-adam-katzenstein" target="_blank"&gt;&lt;em&gt;The Two Saddest Kitchens&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/a&gt; is a comic conversation between cartoonists Roz Chast and Jason Adam Katzenstein about their fear and shame over their apartment kitchens and their disinterest in cooking.&lt;/p&gt;   &lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;🎵 Music: &lt;/strong&gt;Remi Wolf's new album, &lt;em&gt;Mud&lt;/em&gt;, emerged from a period of significant personal change, including a breakup and becoming sober. Watch her &lt;a href="https://www.npr.org/sections/world-cafe/2026/10/13/nx-s1-5998959/remi-wolf-knows-the-best-way-out-of-the-mud-is-through-it" target="_blank"&gt;talk about it and perform some songs&lt;/a&gt; on World Cafe.&lt;/p&gt;   &lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;🎮 Gaming&lt;/strong&gt;: NPR's James Perkins Mastromarino got to play &lt;em&gt;The Legend of Zelda: Ocarina of Time &lt;/em&gt;early, ahead of its Nov. 5 release. He says, "The game's poised to &lt;a href="https://www.npr.org/2026/10/14/nx-s1-5961483/preview-zelda-ocarina-of-time-remake-switch-2" target="_blank"&gt;ensnare old fans and entice new players&lt;/a&gt;."&lt;/p&gt;   &lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;❓ Quiz:&lt;/strong&gt; This week featured changes at the White House, a child reality star's comeback and Elon Musk. If you kept up, &lt;a href="http://npr.org/2026/10/16/g-s1-148041/pope-leo-musk-mamdani-trump-guilfoyle-news-quiz" target="_blank"&gt;you might score perfectly&lt;/a&gt;.&lt;/p&gt;   &lt;h3 class="edTag"&gt;3 things to know before you go&lt;/h3&gt;   &lt;div id="resg-s1-148283" class="bucketwrap image large"&gt;             &lt;div     class="imagewrap has-source-dimensions"     data-crop-type=""     style="         --source-width: 8003;         --source-height: 4502;     " &gt;         &lt;picture&gt;             &lt;source srcset="https://npr.brightspotcdn.com/dims3/default/strip/false/crop/8003x4502+0+417/resize/400/quality/85/format/webp/?url=http%3A%2F%2Fnpr-brightspot.s3.amazonaws.com%2F08%2F37%2F7c03adfa4e89b7205dea8dcf1056%2Fgettyimages-2295968526.jpg 400w, https://npr.brightspotcdn.com/dims3/default/strip/false/crop/8003x4502+0+417/resize/600/quality/85/format/webp/?url=http%3A%2F%2Fnpr-brightspot.s3.amazonaws.com%2F08%2F37%2F7c03adfa4e89b7205dea8dcf1056%2Fgettyimages-2295968526.jpg 600w, https://npr.brightspotcdn.com/dims3/default/strip/false/crop/8003x4502+0+417/resize/800/quality/85/format/webp/?url=http%3A%2F%2Fnpr-brightspot.s3.amazonaws.com%2F08%2F37%2F7c03adfa4e89b7205dea8dcf1056%2Fgettyimages-2295968526.jpg 800w, https://npr.brightspotcdn.com/dims3/default/strip/false/crop/8003x4502+0+417/resize/900/quality/85/format/webp/?url=http%3A%2F%2Fnpr-brightspot.s3.amazonaws.com%2F08%2F37%2F7c03adfa4e89b7205dea8dcf1056%2Fgettyimages-2295968526.jpg 900w, https://npr.brightspotcdn.com/dims3/default/strip/false/crop/8003x4502+0+417/resize/1200/quality/85/format/webp/?url=http%3A%2F%2Fnpr-brightspot.s3.amazonaws.com%2F08%2F37%2F7c03adfa4e89b7205dea8dcf1056%2Fgettyimages-2295968526.jpg 1200w, https://npr.brightspotcdn.com/dims3/default/strip/false/crop/8003x4502+0+417/resize/1600/quality/85/format/webp/?url=http%3A%2F%2Fnpr-brightspot.s3.amazonaws.com%2F08%2F37%2F7c03adfa4e89b7205dea8dcf1056%2Fgettyimages-2295968526.jpg 1600w, https://npr.brightspotcdn.com/dims3/default/strip/false/crop/8003x4502+0+417/resize/1800/quality/85/format/webp/?url=http%3A%2F%2Fnpr-brightspot.s3.amazonaws.com%2F08%2F37%2F7c03adfa4e89b7205dea8dcf1056%2Fgettyimages-2295968526.jpg 1800w" data-template="https://npr.brightspotcdn.com/dims3/default/strip/false/crop/8003x4502+0+417/resize/{width}/quality/{quality}/format/{format}/?url=http%3A%2F%2Fnpr-brightspot.s3.amazonaws.com%2F08%2F37%2F7c03adfa4e89b7205dea8dcf1056%2Fgettyimages-2295968526.jpg" sizes="(min-width: 1025px) 650px, calc(100vw - 30px)" class="img" type="image/webp" /&gt;             &lt;source srcset="https://npr.brightspotcdn.com/dims3/default/strip/false/crop/8003x4502+0+417/resize/400/quality/85/format/jpeg/?url=http%3A%2F%2Fnpr-brightspot.s3.amazonaws.com%2F08%2F37%2F7c03adfa4e89b7205dea8dcf1056%2Fgettyimages-2295968526.jpg 400w, https://npr.brightspotcdn.com/dims3/default/strip/false/crop/8003x4502+0+417/resize/600/quality/85/format/jpeg/?url=http%3A%2F%2Fnpr-brightspot.s3.amazonaws.com%2F08%2F37%2F7c03adfa4e89b7205dea8dcf1056%2Fgettyimages-2295968526.jpg 600w, https://npr.brightspotcdn.com/dims3/default/strip/false/crop/8003x4502+0+417/resize/800/quality/85/format/jpeg/?url=http%3A%2F%2Fnpr-brightspot.s3.amazonaws.com%2F08%2F37%2F7c03adfa4e89b7205dea8dcf1056%2Fgettyimages-2295968526.jpg 800w, https://npr.brightspotcdn.com/dims3/default/strip/false/crop/8003x4502+0+417/resize/900/quality/85/format/jpeg/?url=http%3A%2F%2Fnpr-brightspot.s3.amazonaws.com%2F08%2F37%2F7c03adfa4e89b7205dea8dcf1056%2Fgettyimages-2295968526.jpg 900w, https://npr.brightspotcdn.com/dims3/default/strip/false/crop/8003x4502+0+417/resize/1200/quality/85/format/jpeg/?url=http%3A%2F%2Fnpr-brightspot.s3.amazonaws.com%2F08%2F37%2F7c03adfa4e89b7205dea8dcf1056%2Fgettyimages-2295968526.jpg 1200w, https://npr.brightspotcdn.com/dims3/default/strip/false/crop/8003x4502+0+417/resize/1600/quality/85/format/jpeg/?url=http%3A%2F%2Fnpr-brightspot.s3.amazonaws.com%2F08%2F37%2F7c03adfa4e89b7205dea8dcf1056%2Fgettyimages-2295968526.jpg 1600w, https://npr.brightspotcdn.com/dims3/default/strip/false/crop/8003x4502+0+417/resize/1800/quality/85/format/jpeg/?url=http%3A%2F%2Fnpr-brightspot.s3.amazonaws.com%2F08%2F37%2F7c03adfa4e89b7205dea8dcf1056%2Fgettyimages-2295968526.jpg 1800w" data-template="https://npr.brightspotcdn.com/dims3/default/strip/false/crop/8003x4502+0+417/resize/{width}/quality/{quality}/format/{format}/?url=http%3A%2F%2Fnpr-brightspot.s3.amazonaws.com%2F08%2F37%2F7c03adfa4e89b7205dea8dcf1056%2Fgettyimages-2295968526.jpg" sizes="(min-width: 1025px) 650px, calc(100vw - 30px)" class="img" type="image/jpeg" /&gt;             &lt;img src="https://npr.brightspotcdn.com/dims3/default/strip/false/crop/8003x4502+0+417/resize/1100/quality/50/format/jpeg/?url=http%3A%2F%2Fnpr-brightspot.s3.amazonaws.com%2F08%2F37%2F7c03adfa4e89b7205dea8dcf1056%2Fgettyimages-2295968526.jpg" data-template="https://npr.brightspotcdn.com/dims3/default/strip/false/crop/8003x4502+0+417/resize/{width}/quality/{quality}/format/{format}/?url=http%3A%2F%2Fnpr-brightspot.s3.amazonaws.com%2F08%2F37%2F7c03adfa4e89b7205dea8dcf1056%2Fgettyimages-2295968526.jpg" class="img" alt="Federal authorities are investigating suspicious mailings sent to election officials and congressional offices in multiple states. Above, a USPS mail collection box in Pasadena, Calif." loading="lazy" /&gt;         &lt;/picture&gt; &lt;/div&gt; &lt;div class="credit-caption"&gt;     &lt;div class="caption-wrap"&gt;         &lt;div class="caption" aria-label="Image caption"&gt;             &lt;p&gt;                 Federal authorities are investigating suspicious mailings sent to election officials and congressional offices in multiple states. Above, a USPS mail collection box in Pasadena, Calif.                 &lt;b class="credit" aria-label="Image credit"&gt;                                          Mario Tama/Getty Images                                      &lt;/b&gt;                 &lt;b class="hide-caption"&gt;&lt;b&gt;&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/b&gt;             &lt;/p&gt;         &lt;/div&gt;               &lt;button class="toggle-caption" aria-label=""&gt;               &lt;svg class="icon icon--info"&gt;&lt;use href="#icon-info"&gt;&lt;/use&gt;&lt;/svg&gt;               &lt;b&gt;&lt;/b&gt;                 &lt;abbr title="Toggle Caption" class="toggle-caption__info"&gt;i&lt;/abbr&gt;              &lt;/button&gt;     &lt;/div&gt;       &lt;/div&gt;    &lt;/div&gt;    &lt;ol class="edTag"&gt;&lt;li&gt;The FBI and U.S. Postal Inspection Service are &lt;a href="https://www.npr.org/2026/10/15/nx-s1-6003857/suspicious-mailings-election-congressional-offices" target="_blank"&gt;investigating suspicious mailings&lt;/a&gt;, some of which contained a white powdery substance, to state election officials and congressional offices.&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;Trump has &lt;a href="https://www.npr.org/2026/10/15/nx-s1-6001794/fort-hood-execution-hegseth-christian-nationalist" target="_blank"&gt;canceled the livestream&lt;/a&gt; of Nidal Hasan's execution. The former Army psychiatrist killed 13 people and wounded 32 at Fort Hood, Texas.&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;The Smithsonian National Zoo welcomed five cheetah cubs this month. You can watch them grow and snuggle with their mom on a &lt;a href="https://www.npr.org/2026/10/11/nx-s1-5997459/a-24-hour-livestream-lets-you-watch-adorable-newborn-cheetah-cubs-at-the-national-zoo" target="_blank"&gt;24-hour livestream cheetah cam&lt;/a&gt;.&lt;/li&gt;&lt;/ol&gt;   &lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;This newsletter was edited by &lt;/em&gt;&lt;a href="https://www.npr.org/people/859721331/suzanne-nuyen"target="_blank"   &gt;&lt;em&gt;Suzanne Nuyen&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/a&gt;&lt;em&gt;.&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt; &lt;/div&gt;</description>
