      <title>Social Security benefits to get a boost. And, Hasan Piker defends his rhetoric</title>
      <author>Brittney Melton</author>
      <link>https://www.npr.org/2026/10/15/g-s1-148199/up-first-newsletter-inflation-social-security-ukraine-russia-yemen-saudi-arabia</link>
      <comments>https://text.npr.org/2026/10/15/g-s1-148199/up-first-newsletter-inflation-social-security-ukraine-russia-yemen-saudi-arabia</comments>
      <guid isPermaLink="true">https://www.npr.org/2026/10/15/g-s1-148199/up-first-newsletter-inflation-social-security-ukraine-russia-yemen-saudi-arabia</guid>
      <pubDate>Thu, 15 Oct 2026 11:31:25 +0000</pubDate>
      <description>&lt;div id="storytext" class="storytext storylocation linkLocation"&gt;       &lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;Good morning. You're reading the Up First newsletter. &lt;/em&gt;&lt;a href="https://www.npr.org/newsletter/news" target="_blank"&gt;Subscribe&lt;/a&gt;&lt;em&gt; here to get it delivered to your inbox, and &lt;/em&gt;&lt;a href="https://www.npr.org/podcasts/510318/up-first/" target="_blank"&gt;listen&lt;/a&gt;&lt;em&gt; to the Up First podcast for all the news you need to start your day.&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;   &lt;h3 class="edTag"&gt;Today's top stories&lt;/h3&gt;   &lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Consumer prices in September were 3.7% higher &lt;/strong&gt;than they were a year ago, &lt;a href="https://www.npr.org/2026/10/14/nx-s1-6000593/inflation-consumer-prices-cpi-social-security-benefits" target="_blank"&gt;according to a Labor Department report&lt;/a&gt;. A spike in energy prices linked to the U.S. war with Iran drove up the cost of living. Excluding energy and food prices, core inflation reached 2.6% in September, up from August. The Social Security Administration announced a 3.6% increase in benefits for next year after the release of the inflation report. This annual cost-of-living adjustment is based on prices from July, August and September. Some recipients say the increase is &lt;a href="https://one.npr.org/?sharedMediaId=nx-s1-6001878:x" target="_blank"&gt;not enough&lt;/a&gt;.&lt;/p&gt;   &lt;div id="resg-s1-147910" class="bucketwrap image large"&gt;             &lt;div     class="imagewrap has-source-dimensions"     data-crop-type=""     style="         --source-width: 5000;         --source-height: 2813;     " &gt;         &lt;picture&gt;             &lt;source srcset="https://npr.brightspotcdn.com/dims3/default/strip/false/crop/5000x2813+0+260/resize/400/quality/85/format/webp/?url=http%3A%2F%2Fnpr-brightspot.s3.amazonaws.com%2F56%2F61%2Fc0ae826a434f85125c7d6ab98c31%2Fgettyimages-2298003777.jpg 400w, https://npr.brightspotcdn.com/dims3/default/strip/false/crop/5000x2813+0+260/resize/600/quality/85/format/webp/?url=http%3A%2F%2Fnpr-brightspot.s3.amazonaws.com%2F56%2F61%2Fc0ae826a434f85125c7d6ab98c31%2Fgettyimages-2298003777.jpg 600w, https://npr.brightspotcdn.com/dims3/default/strip/false/crop/5000x2813+0+260/resize/800/quality/85/format/webp/?url=http%3A%2F%2Fnpr-brightspot.s3.amazonaws.com%2F56%2F61%2Fc0ae826a434f85125c7d6ab98c31%2Fgettyimages-2298003777.jpg 800w, https://npr.brightspotcdn.com/dims3/default/strip/false/crop/5000x2813+0+260/resize/900/quality/85/format/webp/?url=http%3A%2F%2Fnpr-brightspot.s3.amazonaws.com%2F56%2F61%2Fc0ae826a434f85125c7d6ab98c31%2Fgettyimages-2298003777.jpg 900w, https://npr.brightspotcdn.com/dims3/default/strip/false/crop/5000x2813+0+260/resize/1200/quality/85/format/webp/?url=http%3A%2F%2Fnpr-brightspot.s3.amazonaws.com%2F56%2F61%2Fc0ae826a434f85125c7d6ab98c31%2Fgettyimages-2298003777.jpg 1200w, https://npr.brightspotcdn.com/dims3/default/strip/false/crop/5000x2813+0+260/resize/1600/quality/85/format/webp/?url=http%3A%2F%2Fnpr-brightspot.s3.amazonaws.com%2F56%2F61%2Fc0ae826a434f85125c7d6ab98c31%2Fgettyimages-2298003777.jpg 1600w, https://npr.brightspotcdn.com/dims3/default/strip/false/crop/5000x2813+0+260/resize/1800/quality/85/format/webp/?url=http%3A%2F%2Fnpr-brightspot.s3.amazonaws.com%2F56%2F61%2Fc0ae826a434f85125c7d6ab98c31%2Fgettyimages-2298003777.jpg 1800w" data-template="https://npr.brightspotcdn.com/dims3/default/strip/false/crop/5000x2813+0+260/resize/{width}/quality/{quality}/format/{format}/?url=http%3A%2F%2Fnpr-brightspot.s3.amazonaws.com%2F56%2F61%2Fc0ae826a434f85125c7d6ab98c31%2Fgettyimages-2298003777.jpg" sizes="(min-width: 1025px) 650px, calc(100vw - 30px)" class="img" type="image/webp" /&gt;             &lt;source srcset="https://npr.brightspotcdn.com/dims3/default/strip/false/crop/5000x2813+0+260/resize/400/quality/85/format/jpeg/?url=http%3A%2F%2Fnpr-brightspot.s3.amazonaws.com%2F56%2F61%2Fc0ae826a434f85125c7d6ab98c31%2Fgettyimages-2298003777.jpg 400w, https://npr.brightspotcdn.com/dims3/default/strip/false/crop/5000x2813+0+260/resize/600/quality/85/format/jpeg/?url=http%3A%2F%2Fnpr-brightspot.s3.amazonaws.com%2F56%2F61%2Fc0ae826a434f85125c7d6ab98c31%2Fgettyimages-2298003777.jpg 600w, https://npr.brightspotcdn.com/dims3/default/strip/false/crop/5000x2813+0+260/resize/800/quality/85/format/jpeg/?url=http%3A%2F%2Fnpr-brightspot.s3.amazonaws.com%2F56%2F61%2Fc0ae826a434f85125c7d6ab98c31%2Fgettyimages-2298003777.jpg 800w, https://npr.brightspotcdn.com/dims3/default/strip/false/crop/5000x2813+0+260/resize/900/quality/85/format/jpeg/?url=http%3A%2F%2Fnpr-brightspot.s3.amazonaws.com%2F56%2F61%2Fc0ae826a434f85125c7d6ab98c31%2Fgettyimages-2298003777.jpg 900w, https://npr.brightspotcdn.com/dims3/default/strip/false/crop/5000x2813+0+260/resize/1200/quality/85/format/jpeg/?url=http%3A%2F%2Fnpr-brightspot.s3.amazonaws.com%2F56%2F61%2Fc0ae826a434f85125c7d6ab98c31%2Fgettyimages-2298003777.jpg 1200w, https://npr.brightspotcdn.com/dims3/default/strip/false/crop/5000x2813+0+260/resize/1600/quality/85/format/jpeg/?url=http%3A%2F%2Fnpr-brightspot.s3.amazonaws.com%2F56%2F61%2Fc0ae826a434f85125c7d6ab98c31%2Fgettyimages-2298003777.jpg 1600w, https://npr.brightspotcdn.com/dims3/default/strip/false/crop/5000x2813+0+260/resize/1800/quality/85/format/jpeg/?url=http%3A%2F%2Fnpr-brightspot.s3.amazonaws.com%2F56%2F61%2Fc0ae826a434f85125c7d6ab98c31%2Fgettyimages-2298003777.jpg 1800w" data-template="https://npr.brightspotcdn.com/dims3/default/strip/false/crop/5000x2813+0+260/resize/{width}/quality/{quality}/format/{format}/?url=http%3A%2F%2Fnpr-brightspot.s3.amazonaws.com%2F56%2F61%2Fc0ae826a434f85125c7d6ab98c31%2Fgettyimages-2298003777.jpg" sizes="(min-width: 1025px) 650px, calc(100vw - 30px)" class="img" type="image/jpeg" /&gt;             &lt;img src="https://npr.brightspotcdn.com/dims3/default/strip/false/crop/5000x2813+0+260/resize/1100/quality/50/format/jpeg/?url=http%3A%2F%2Fnpr-brightspot.s3.amazonaws.com%2F56%2F61%2Fc0ae826a434f85125c7d6ab98c31%2Fgettyimages-2298003777.jpg" data-template="https://npr.brightspotcdn.com/dims3/default/strip/false/crop/5000x2813+0+260/resize/{width}/quality/{quality}/format/{format}/?url=http%3A%2F%2Fnpr-brightspot.s3.amazonaws.com%2F56%2F61%2Fc0ae826a434f85125c7d6ab98c31%2Fgettyimages-2298003777.jpg" class="img" alt="A man pumps gas at a gas station." loading="lazy" /&gt;         &lt;/picture&gt; &lt;/div&gt; &lt;div class="credit-caption"&gt;     &lt;div class="caption-wrap"&gt;         &lt;div class="caption" aria-label="Image caption"&gt;             &lt;p&gt;                 Rising gasoline and diesel prices pushed inflation higher in September. The cost of living index was up 3.7%, according to a report Wednesday from the Labor Department.                 &lt;b class="credit" aria-label="Image credit"&gt;                                          Isabelle Souriment/Hans Lucas/AFP via Getty Images                                      &lt;/b&gt;                 &lt;b class="hide-caption"&gt;&lt;b&gt;&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/b&gt;             &lt;/p&gt;         &lt;/div&gt;               &lt;button class="toggle-caption" aria-label=""&gt;               &lt;svg class="icon icon--info"&gt;&lt;use href="#icon-info"&gt;&lt;/use&gt;&lt;/svg&gt;               &lt;b&gt;&lt;/b&gt;                 &lt;abbr title="Toggle Caption" class="toggle-caption__info"&gt;i&lt;/abbr&gt;              &lt;/button&gt;     &lt;/div&gt;       &lt;/div&gt;    &lt;/div&gt;    &lt;ul class="edTag"&gt;&lt;li&gt;🎧 &lt;strong&gt;Social Security may run out of money&lt;/strong&gt; to make full payments to retirees as soon as 2032. NPR's &lt;em&gt;Planet Money&lt;/em&gt; &lt;a href="https://one.npr.org/?sharedMediaId=nx-s1-6000635:x" target="_blank"&gt;examines possible solutions&lt;/a&gt;.&lt;/li&gt;&lt;/ul&gt;   &lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Ukrainian President Volodymyr Zelenskyy announced he will resume attacks &lt;/strong&gt;on Russian oil refineries, despite President Trump's request to refrain from doing so. Zelenskyy told the &lt;em&gt;Financial Times &lt;/em&gt;that he had ordered commanders to stand down earlier this week, but wouldn't anymore. But Ukraine's ability to conduct these long-range attacks may be limited, as it has seen sudden crippling restrictions to Starshield, the satellite communications system provided by the U.S.&lt;br&gt;&lt;/p&gt;       &lt;ul class="edTag"&gt;&lt;li&gt;🎧&lt;strong&gt; The U.S. is seemingly trying to limit Ukraine's ability to fight Russia&lt;/strong&gt;, though that has not been announced outright, NPR's Greg Myre tells &lt;em&gt;Up First&lt;/em&gt;. Ukraine's defense ministry said today that operations are back to normal. The country relies on the Starshield system for offensive and defensive drones to &lt;a href="http://one.npr.org/i/nx-s1-6003418:x" target="_blank"&gt;protect against Russian strikes&lt;/a&gt;. Elon Musk, who developed the system for the U.S. government and military, says the U.S. government sets its speed and usage limits.&lt;/li&gt;&lt;/ul&gt;   &lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;A man shot and wounded by U.S. Immigration and Customs Enforcement agents &lt;/strong&gt;in New York last week says he didn't know the men who shot him were ICE agents until after he woke up in the hospital. A &lt;a href="https://gothamist.com/news/man-shot-by-ice-in-nycs-marble-hill-said-federal-officers-never-identified-themselves" target="_blank"&gt;new petition filed&lt;/a&gt; in Brooklyn federal court says the agents — many of them masked — didn't identify themselves before approaching Oscar Belgal's vehicle with their firearms drawn. The filing contradicts the Trump administration's version of events.&lt;/p&gt;   &lt;h3 class="edTag"&gt;Watch this&lt;/h3&gt;   &lt;div id="resg-s1-148190" class="bucketwrap image large"&gt;             &lt;div     class="imagewrap has-source-dimensions"     data-crop-type=""     style="         --source-width: 2600;         --source-height: 1463;     " &gt;         &lt;picture&gt;             &lt;sourc