100vw - 30px)" class="img" type="image/webp" /&gt;             &lt;source srcset="https://npr.brightspotcdn.com/dims3/default/strip/false/crop/2600x1463+0+0/resize/400/quality/85/format/png/?url=http%3A%2F%2Fnpr-brightspot.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fff%2F79%2Fde3419ae462a9725c4b204ca74c2%2Fnewsmakers-hasanpiker-clean.png 400w, https://npr.brightspotcdn.com/dims3/default/strip/false/crop/2600x1463+0+0/resize/600/quality/85/format/png/?url=http%3A%2F%2Fnpr-brightspot.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fff%2F79%2Fde3419ae462a9725c4b204ca74c2%2Fnewsmakers-hasanpiker-clean.png 600w, https://npr.brightspotcdn.com/dims3/default/strip/false/crop/2600x1463+0+0/resize/800/quality/85/format/png/?url=http%3A%2F%2Fnpr-brightspot.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fff%2F79%2Fde3419ae462a9725c4b204ca74c2%2Fnewsmakers-hasanpiker-clean.png 800w, https://npr.brightspotcdn.com/dims3/default/strip/false/crop/2600x1463+0+0/resize/900/quality/85/format/png/?url=http%3A%2F%2Fnpr-brightspot.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fff%2F79%2Fde3419ae462a9725c4b204ca74c2%2Fnewsmakers-hasanpiker-clean.png 900w, https://npr.brightspotcdn.com/dims3/default/strip/false/crop/2600x1463+0+0/resize/1200/quality/85/format/png/?url=http%3A%2F%2Fnpr-brightspot.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fff%2F79%2Fde3419ae462a9725c4b204ca74c2%2Fnewsmakers-hasanpiker-clean.png 1200w, https://npr.brightspotcdn.com/dims3/default/strip/false/crop/2600x1463+0+0/resize/1600/quality/85/format/png/?url=http%3A%2F%2Fnpr-brightspot.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fff%2F79%2Fde3419ae462a9725c4b204ca74c2%2Fnewsmakers-hasanpiker-clean.png 1600w, https://npr.brightspotcdn.com/dims3/default/strip/false/crop/2600x1463+0+0/resize/1800/quality/85/format/png/?url=http%3A%2F%2Fnpr-brightspot.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fff%2F79%2Fde3419ae462a9725c4b204ca74c2%2Fnewsmakers-hasanpiker-clean.png 1800w" data-template="https://npr.brightspotcdn.com/dims3/default/strip/false/crop/2600x1463+0+0/resize/{width}/quality/{quality}/format/{format}/?url=http%3A%2F%2Fnpr-brightspot.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fff%2F79%2Fde3419ae462a9725c4b204ca74c2%2Fnewsmakers-hasanpiker-clean.png" sizes="(min-width: 1025px) 650px, calc(100vw - 30px)" class="img" type="image/png" /&gt;             &lt;img src="https://npr.brightspotcdn.com/dims3/default/strip/false/crop/2600x1463+0+0/resize/1100/quality/50/format/png/?url=http%3A%2F%2Fnpr-brightspot.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fff%2F79%2Fde3419ae462a9725c4b204ca74c2%2Fnewsmakers-hasanpiker-clean.png" data-template="https://npr.brightspotcdn.com/dims3/default/strip/false/crop/2600x1463+0+0/resize/{width}/quality/{quality}/format/{format}/?url=http%3A%2F%2Fnpr-brightspot.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fff%2F79%2Fde3419ae462a9725c4b204ca74c2%2Fnewsmakers-hasanpiker-clean.png" class="img" alt="Hasan Piker is seen from the shoulders up wearing a light brown suit jacket. " loading="lazy" /&gt;         &lt;/picture&gt; &lt;/div&gt; &lt;div class="credit-caption"&gt;     &lt;div class="caption-wrap"&gt;         &lt;div class="caption" aria-label="Image caption"&gt;         &lt;/div&gt;       &lt;/div&gt;       &lt;/div&gt;    &lt;/div&gt;    &lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;Go face-to-face with the person of the moment. NPR's &lt;/em&gt;Newsmakers&lt;em&gt; video podcast brings the biggest names in politics, business, sports, arts, and culture out of the headlines and into the interview chair to discuss the mark they're making on the world. Follow the &lt;/em&gt;&lt;a href="https://www.npr.org/podcasts/g-s1-114952/nprs-newsmakers" target="_blank"&gt;Newsmakers&lt;em&gt; podcast&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/a&gt;&lt;em&gt; or subscribe to &lt;/em&gt;&lt;a href="https://www.youtube.com/npr" target="_blank"&gt;&lt;em&gt;NPR's YouTube channel&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/a&gt;&lt;em&gt; to get new episodes as soon as they're available.&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;   &lt;p&gt;California-based Twitch streamer Hasan Piker has emerged as a key target for the GOP ahead of the midterm elections. The president recently labeled him a "terrible liability" and a "communist." In Michigan, political ads attempting to link him to Democratic candidate Abdul El-Sayef repeatedly play Piker's most controversial statements, including the infamous "America deserved 9/11." Piker remains confident that he won't hinder Democrats this November. In a conversation with &lt;em&gt;Morning Edition&lt;/em&gt;'s Leila Fadel, he reflects on his past remarks, the loneliness young men feel and his critique of Tucker Carlson.&lt;/p&gt;       &lt;aside id="mid-story-recommendations-mount-piano" class="mid-story-recommendations-mount-piano" aria-label="recommended stories"&gt;&lt;/aside&gt;    &lt;!-- END ID="MID-STORY-RECOMMENDATIONS-MOUNT-PIANO" CLASS="MID-STORY-RECOMMENDATIONS-MOUNT-PIANO" ARIA-LABEL="RECOMMENDED STORIES" --&gt;    &lt;p&gt;&lt;a href="https://lnk.to/iXWQLdNW" target="_blank"&gt;Watch or listen&lt;/a&gt; to the interview or &lt;a href="http://npr.org/2026/10/15/nx-s1-5950023/hasan-piker-midterms-democrats-rhetoric" target="_blank"&gt;read the article&lt;/a&gt; about their discussion.&lt;/p&gt;   &lt;h3 class="edTag"&gt;Picture show&lt;/h3&gt;   &lt;div id="resg-s1-147365" class="bucketwrap image large"&gt;             &lt;div     class="imagewrap has-source-dimensions"     data-crop-type=""     style="         --source-width: 3611;         --source-height: 2032;     " &gt;         &lt;picture&gt;             &lt;source srcset="https://npr.brightspotcdn.com/dims3/default/strip/false/crop/3611x2032+723+588/resize/400/quality/85/format/webp/?url=http%3A%2F%2Fnpr-brightspot.s3.amazonaws.com%2F93%2Ff9%2F95c95135429ebedfe105ffea3126%2Ftoddlerdjlennypearce-554.jpg 400w, https://npr.brightspotcdn.com/dims3/default/strip/false/crop/3611x2032+723+588/resize/600/quality/85/format/webp/?url=http%3A%2F%2Fnpr-brightspot.s3.amazonaws.com%2F93%2Ff9%2F95c95135429ebedfe105ffea3126%2Ftoddlerdjlennypearce-554.jpg 600w, https://npr.brightspotcdn.com/dims3/default/strip/false/crop/3611x2032+723+588/resize/800/quality/85/format/webp/?url=http%3A%2F%2Fnpr-brightspot.s3.amazonaws.com%2F93%2Ff9%2F95c95135429ebedfe105ffea3126%2Ftoddlerdjlennypearce-554.jpg 800w, https://npr.brightspotcdn.com/dims3/default/strip/false/crop/3611x2032+723+588/resize/900/quality/85/format/webp/?url=http%3A%2F%2Fnpr-brightspot.s3.amazonaws.com%2F93%2Ff9%2F95c95135429ebedfe105ffea3126%2Ftoddlerdjlennypearce-554.jpg 900w, https://npr.brightspotcdn.com/dims3/default/strip/false/crop/3611x2032+723+588/resize/1200/quality/85/format/webp/?url=http%3A%2F%2Fnpr-brightspot.s3.amazonaws.com%2F93%2Ff9%2F95c95135429ebedfe105ffea3126%2Ftoddlerdjlennypearce-554.jpg 1200w, https://npr.brightspotcdn.com/dims3/default/strip/false/crop/3611x2032+723+588/resize/1600/quality/85/format/webp/?url=http%3A%2F%2Fnpr-brightspot.s3.amazonaws.com%2F93%2Ff9%2F95c95135429ebedfe105ffea3126%2Ftoddlerdjlennypearce-554.jpg 1600w, https://npr.brightspotcdn.com/dims3/default/strip/false/crop/3611x2032+723+588/resize/1800/quality/85/format/webp/?url=http%3A%2F%2Fnpr-brightspot.s3.amazonaws.com%2F93%2Ff9%2F95c95135429ebedfe105ffea3126%2Ftoddlerdjlennypearce-554.jpg 1800w" data-template="https://npr.brightspotcdn.com/dims3/default/strip/false/crop/3611x2032+723+588/resize/{width}/quality/{quality}/format/{format}/?url=http%3A%2F%2Fnpr-brightspot.s3.amazonaws.com%2F93%2Ff9%2F95c95135429ebedfe105ffea3126%2Ftoddlerdjlennypearce-554.jpg" sizes="(min-width: 1025px) 650px, calc(100vw - 30px)" class="img" type="image/webp" /&gt;             &lt;source srcset="https://npr.brightspotcdn.com/dims3/default/strip/false/crop/3611x2032+723+588/resize/400/quality/85/format/jpeg/?url=http%3A%2F%2Fnpr-brightspot.s3.amazonaws.com%2F93%2Ff9%2F95c95135429ebedfe105ffea3126%2Ftoddlerdjlennypearce-554.jpg 400w, https://npr.brightspotcdn.com/dims3/default/strip/false/crop/3611x2032+723+588/resize/600/quality/85/format/jpeg/?url=http%3A%2F%2Fnpr-brightspot.s3.amazonaws.com%2F93%2Ff9%2F95c95135429ebedfe105ffea3126%2Ftoddlerdjlennypearce-554.jpg 600w, https://npr.brightspotcdn.com/dims3/default/strip/false/crop/3611x2032+723+588/resize/800/quality/85/format/jpeg/?url=http%3A%2F%2Fnpr-brightspot.s3.amazonaws.com%2F93%2Ff9%2F95c95135429ebedfe105ffea3126%2Ftoddlerdjlennypearce-554.jpg 800w, https://npr.brightspotcdn.com/dims3/default/strip/false/crop/3611x2032+723+588/resize/900/quality/85/format/jpeg/?url=http%3A%2F%2Fnpr-brightspot.s3.amazonaws.com%2F93%2Ff9%2F95c95135429ebedfe105ffea3126%2Ftoddlerdjlennypearce-554.jpg 900w, https://npr.brightspotcdn.com/dims3/default/strip/false/crop/3611x2032+723+588/resize/1200/quality/85/format/jpeg/?url=http%3A%2F%2Fnpr-brightspot.s3.amazonaws.com%2F93%2Ff9%2F95c95135429ebedfe105ffea3126%2Ftoddlerdjlennypearce-554.jpg 1200w, https://npr.brightspotcdn.com/dims3/default/strip/false/crop/3611x2032+723+588/resize/1600/quality/85/format/jpeg/?url=http%3A%2F%2Fnpr-brightspot.s3.amazonaws.com%2F93%2Ff9%2F95c95135429ebedfe105ffea3126%2Ftoddlerdjlennypearce-554.jpg 1600w, https://npr.brightspotcdn.com/dims3/default/strip/false/crop/3611x2032+723+588/resize/1800/quality/85/format/jpeg/?url=http%3A%2F%2Fnpr-brightspot.s3.amazonaws.com%2F93%2Ff9%2F95c95135429ebedfe105ffea3126%2Ftoddlerdjlennypearce-554.jpg 1800w" data-template="https://npr.brightspotcdn.com/dims3/default/strip/false/crop/3611x2032+723+588/resize/{width}/quality/{quality}/format/{format}/?url=http%3A%2F%2Fnpr-brightspot.s3.amazonaws.com%2F93%2Ff9%2F95c95135429ebedfe105ffea3126%2Ftoddlerdjlennypearce-554.jpg" sizes="(min-width: 1025px) 650px, calc(100vw - 30px)" class="img" type="image/jpeg" /&gt;             &lt;img src="https://npr.brightspotcdn.com/dims3/default/strip/false/crop/3611x2032+723+588/resize/1100/quality/50/format/jpeg/?url=http%3A%2F%2Fnpr-brightspot.s3.amazonaws.com%2F93%2Ff9%2F95c95135429ebedfe105ffea3126%2Ftoddlerdjlennypearce-554.jpg" data-template="https://npr.brightspotcdn.com/dims3/default/strip/false/crop/3611x2032+723+588/resize/{width}/quality/{quality}/format/{format}/?url=http%3A%2F%2Fnpr-brightspot.s3.amazonaws.com%2F93%2Ff9%2F95c95135429ebedfe105ffea3126%2Ftoddlerdjlennypearce-554.jpg" class="img" alt="Australian DJ Lenny Pearce performs in Baltimore." loading="lazy" /&gt;         &lt;/picture&gt; &lt;/div&gt; &lt;div class="credit-caption"&gt;     &lt;div class="caption-wrap"&gt;         &lt;div class="caption" aria-label="Image caption"&gt;             &lt;p&gt;                 Australian DJ Lenny Pearce performs in Baltimore.                 &lt;b class="credit" aria-label="Image credit"&gt;                                          KT Kanazawich for NPR                                      &lt;/b&gt;                 &lt;b class="hide-caption"&gt;&lt;b&gt;&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/b&gt;             &lt;/p&gt;         &lt;/div&gt;               &lt;button class="toggle-caption" aria-label=""&gt;               &lt;svg class="icon icon--info"&gt;&lt;use href="#icon-info"&gt;&lt;/use&gt;&lt;/svg&gt;               &lt;b&gt;&lt;/b&gt;                 &lt;abbr title="Toggle Caption" class="toggle-caption__info"&gt;i&lt;/abbr&gt;              &lt;/button&gt;     &lt;/div&gt;       &lt;/div&gt;    &lt;/div&gt;    &lt;p&gt;Australian DJ Lenny Pearce is taking over venues with his toddler rave world tour. Yes, it's is exactly what it sounds like: techno dance parties for families. Most of the dance floor is filled with little ones under the age of five. Around 5 p.m., the speakers blast nursery rhymes like "Bingo" and "The Wheels on the Bus," while the bar offers a refreshing house specialty: apple juice. Pearce kicked off the North American leg of his tour in Baltimore, but has sold-out shows in cities such as New York and Los Angeles and has already captivated audiences in Bahrain, Singapore and India. Take a look at these photos of the &lt;a href="https://www.npr.org/2026/10/04/nx-s1-5872210/at-this-rave-the-crowd-is-under-5-and-home-by-bedtime" target="_blank"&gt;young ravers at his events&lt;/a&gt;.&lt;/p&gt;   &lt;h3 class="edTag"&gt;3 things to know before you go&lt;/h3&gt;   &lt;div id="resg-s1-147517" class="bucketwrap image large"&gt;             &lt;div     class="imagewrap has-source-dimensions"     data-crop-type=""     style="         --source-width: 3000;         --source-height: 1688;     " &gt;         &lt;picture&gt;             &lt;source srcset="https://npr.brightspotcdn.com/dims3/default/strip/false/crop/3000x1688+0+313/resize/400/quality/85/format/webp/?url=http%3A%2F%2Fnpr-brightspot.s3.amazonaws.com%2F6d%2F2f%2F30744d4d4596978ebb8523f3e468%2F20260509-dsc7811.jpg 400w, https://npr.brightspotcdn.com/dims3/default/strip/false/crop/3000x1688+0+313/resize/600/quality/85/format/webp/?url=http%3A%2F%2Fnpr-brightspot.s3.amazonaws.com%2F6d%2F2f%2F30744d4d4596978ebb8523f3e468%2F20260509-dsc7811.jpg 600w, https://npr.brightspotcdn.com/dims3/default/strip/false/crop/3000x1688+0+313/resize/800/quality/85/format/webp/?url=http%3A%2F%2Fnpr-brightspot.s3.amazonaws.com%2F6d%2F2f%2F30744d4d4596978ebb8523f3e468%2F20260509-dsc7811.jpg 800w, https://npr.brightspotcdn.com/dims3/default/strip/false/crop/3000x1688+0+313/resize/900/quality/85/format/webp/?url=http%3A%2F%2Fnpr-brightspot.s3.amazonaws.com%2F6d%2F2f%2F30744d4d4596978ebb8523f3e468%2F20260509-dsc7811.jpg 900w, https://npr.brightspotcdn.com/dims3/default/strip/false/crop/3000x1688+0+313/resize/1200/quality/85/format/webp/?url=http%3A%2F%2Fnpr-brightspot.s3.amazonaws.com%2F6d%2F2f%2F30744d4d4596978ebb8523f3e468%2F20260509-dsc7811.jpg 1200w, https://npr.brightspotcdn.com/dims3/default/strip/false/crop/3000x1688+0+313/resize/1600/quality/85/format/webp/?url=http%3A%2F%2Fnpr-brightspot.s3.amazonaws.com%2F6d%2F2f%2F30744d4d4596978ebb8523f3e468%2F20260509-dsc7811.jpg 1600w, https://npr.brightspotcdn.com/dims3/default/strip/false/crop/3000x1688+0+313/resize/1800/quality/85/format/webp/?url=http%3A%2F%2Fnpr-brightspot.s3.amazonaws.com%2F6d%2F2f%2F30744d4d4596978ebb8523f3e468%2F20260509-dsc7811.jpg 1800w" data-template="https://npr.brightspotcdn.com/dims3/default/strip/false/crop/3000x1688+0+313/resize/{width}/quality/{quality}/format/{format}/?url=http%3A%2F%2Fnpr-brightspot.s3.amazonaws.com%2F6d%2F2f%2F30744d4d4596978ebb8523f3e468%2F20260509-dsc7811.jpg" sizes="(min-width: 1025px) 650px, calc(100vw - 30px)" class="img" type="image/webp" /&gt;             &lt;source srcset="https://npr.brightspotcdn.com/dims3/default/strip/false/crop/3000x1688+0+313/resize/400/quality/85/format/jpeg/?url=http%3A%2F%2Fnpr-brightspot.s3.amazonaws.com%2F6d%2F2f%2F30744d4d4596978ebb8523f3e468%2F20260509-dsc7811.jpg 400w, https://npr.brightspotcdn.com/dims3/default/strip/false/crop/3000x1688+0+313/resize/600/quality/85/format/jpeg/?url=http%3A%2F%2Fnpr-brightspot.s3.amazonaws.com%2F6d%2F2f%2F30744d4d4596978ebb8523f3e468%2F20260509-dsc7811.jpg 600w, https://npr.brightspotcdn.com/dims3/default/strip/false/crop/3000x1688+0+313/resize/800/quality/85/format/jpeg/?url=http%3A%2F%2Fnpr-brightspot.s3.amazonaws.com%2F6d%2F2f%2F30744d4d4596978ebb8523f3e468%2F20260509-dsc7811.jpg 800w, https://npr.brightspotcdn.com/dims3/default/strip/false/crop/3000x1688+0+313/resize/900/quality/85/format/jpeg/?url=http%3A%2F%2Fnpr-brightspot.s3.amazonaws.com%2F6d%2F2f%2F30744d4d4596978ebb8523f3e468%2F20260509-dsc7811.jpg 900w, https://npr.brightspotcdn.com/dims3/default/strip/false/crop/3000x1688+0+313/resize/1200/quality/85/format/jpeg/?url=http%3A%2F%2Fnpr-brightspot.s3.amazonaws.com%2F6d%2F2f%2F30744d4d4596978ebb8523f3e468%2F20260509-dsc7811.jpg 1200w, https://npr.brightspotcdn.com/dims3/default/strip/false/crop/3000x1688+0+313/resize/1600/quality/85/format/jpeg/?url=http%3A%2F%2Fnpr-brightspot.s3.amazonaws.com%2F6d%2F2f%2F30744d4d4596978ebb8523f3e468%2F20260509-dsc7811.jpg 1600w, https://npr.brightspotcdn.com/dims3/default/strip/false/crop/3000x1688+0+313/resize/1800/quality/85/format/jpeg/?url=http%3A%2F%2Fnpr-brightspot.s3.amazonaws.com%2F6d%2F2f%2F30744d4d4596978ebb8523f3e468%2F20260509-dsc7811.jpg 1800w" data-template="https://npr.brightspotcdn.com/dims3/default/strip/false/crop/3000x1688+0+313/resize/{width}/quality/{quality}/format/{format}/?url=http%3A%2F%2Fnpr-brightspot.s3.amazonaws.com%2F6d%2F2f%2F30744d4d4596978ebb8523f3e468%2F20260509-dsc7811.jpg" sizes="(min-width: 1025px) 650px, calc(100vw - 30px)" class="img" type="image/jpeg" /&gt;             &lt;img src="https://npr.brightspotcdn.com/dims3/default/strip/false/crop/3000x1688+0+313/resize/1100/quality/50/format/jpeg/?url=http%3A%2F%2Fnpr-brightspot.s3.amazonaws.com%2F6d%2F2f%2F30744d4d4596978ebb8523f3e468%2F20260509-dsc7811.jpg" data-template="https://npr.brightspotcdn.com/dims3/default/strip/false/crop/3000x1688+0+313/resize/{width}/quality/{quality}/format/{format}/?url=http%3A%2F%2Fnpr-brightspot.s3.amazonaws.com%2F6d%2F2f%2F30744d4d4596978ebb8523f3e468%2F20260509-dsc7811.jpg" class="img" alt="At Palmyra Atoll in the remote Pacific Ocean, wildlife refuge manager Paige Mino observes red-footed boobies. Scientists have found a surprising link between the seabirds and the health of the surrounding ocean." loading="lazy" /&gt;         &lt;/picture&gt; &lt;/div&gt; &lt;div class="credit-caption"&gt;     &lt;div class="caption-wrap"&gt;         &lt;div class="caption" aria-label="Image caption"&gt;             &lt;p&gt;                 At Palmyra Atoll in the remote Pacific Ocean, wildlife refuge manager Paige Mino observes red-footed boobies. Scientists have found a surprising link between the seabirds and the health of the surrounding ocean.                 &lt;b class="credit" aria-label="Image credit"&gt;                                          Claire Harbage/NPR                                      &lt;/b&gt;                 &lt;b class="hide-caption"&gt;&lt;b&gt;&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/b&gt;             &lt;/p&gt;         &lt;/div&gt;               &lt;button class="toggle-caption" aria-label=""&gt;               &lt;svg class="icon icon--info"&gt;&lt;use href="#icon-info"&gt;&lt;/use&gt;&lt;/svg&gt;               &lt;b&gt;&lt;/b&gt;                 &lt;abbr title="Toggle Caption" class="toggle-caption__info"&gt;i&lt;/abbr&gt;              &lt;/button&gt;     &lt;/div&gt;       &lt;/div&gt;    &lt;/div&gt;    &lt;ol class="edTag"&gt;&lt;li&gt;Coral reefs worldwide face rising threats. On a remote Pacific island, scientists discovered that &lt;a href="https://www.npr.org/2026/10/13/nx-s1-5901320/coral-reefs-palmyra-atoll-birds-restoration" target="_blank"&gt;seabirds can help them&lt;/a&gt;.&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;The New York City Council and Mayor Zohran Mamdani announced plans to &lt;a href="https://gothamist.com/news/nyc-council-set-to-ban-central-parks-carriage-horse-industry" target="_blank"&gt;ban carriage horses in Central Park&lt;/a&gt;. (via &lt;a href="https://gothamist.com/" target="_blank"&gt;Gothamist&lt;/a&gt;)&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;NPR's Eyder Peralta takes readers to a Mexico City park in the &lt;a href="http://npr.org/2026/10/15/nx-s1-6001550/mexico-city-bullfighting-ban-matador-training" target="_blank"&gt;latest installment of Far-Flung Postcards&lt;/a&gt;. There, people still practice bullfighting, even though it is banned.&lt;/li&gt;&lt;/ol&gt;   &lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;This newsletter was edited by &lt;/em&gt;&lt;a href="https://www.npr.org/people/859721331/suzanne-nuyen"target="_blank"   &gt;&lt;em&gt;Suzanne Nuyen&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/a&gt;&lt;em&gt;.&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt; &lt;/div&gt;</description>
      <media:content url="https://prfx.byspotify.com/e/play.podtrac.com/npr-510318/npr.simplecastaudio.com/d52bee4a-b10a-40f8-9417-45064e6b8632/episodes/face723b-c120-4b3c-8023-2ccb1c2b6ea6/audio/128/default.mp3?awCollectionId=d52bee4a-b10a-40f8-9417-45064e6b8632&amp;amp;awEpisodeId=face723b-c120-4b3c-8023-2ccb1c2b6ea6&amp;amp;feed=HMwRVgVt&amp;amp;t=podcast&amp;amp;e=nx-s1-6003418&amp;amp;p=510318&amp;amp;d=808&amp;amp;size=12942986&amp;amp;sc=siteplayer&amp;amp;aw_0_1st.playerid=siteplayer" type="audio/mpeg"/>
