      <title>Government spent millions on Trump ads. And, federal agents raid Ilhan Omar's home</title>
      <author>Brittney Melton</author>
      <link>https://www.npr.org/2026/10/13/g-s1-147822/up-first-newsletter-trump-ads-funding-campaign-rallies-ilhan-omar</link>
      <comments>https://text.npr.org/2026/10/13/g-s1-147822/up-first-newsletter-trump-ads-funding-campaign-rallies-ilhan-omar</comments>
      <guid isPermaLink="true">https://www.npr.org/2026/10/13/g-s1-147822/up-first-newsletter-trump-ads-funding-campaign-rallies-ilhan-omar</guid>
      <pubDate>Tue, 13 Oct 2026 11:08:14 +0000</pubDate>
      <description>&lt;div id="storytext" class="storytext storylocation linkLocation"&gt;       &lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;Good morning. You're reading the Up First newsletter. &lt;/em&gt;&lt;a href="https://www.npr.org/newsletter/news" target="_blank"&gt;Subscribe&lt;/a&gt;&lt;em&gt; here to get it delivered to your inbox, and &lt;/em&gt;&lt;a href="https://www.npr.org/podcasts/510318/up-first/" target="_blank"&gt;listen&lt;/a&gt;&lt;em&gt; to the Up First podcast for all the news you need to start your day.&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;   &lt;h3 class="edTag"&gt;Today's top stories&lt;/h3&gt;   &lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;The U.S. government continues to pay for ads promoting President Trump&lt;/strong&gt;, even after he announced that his MAGA Inc. super PAC would take over funding. A federal judge ordered the ads to be taken down, yet they remained on air. An NPR analysis of data from AdImpact finds that &lt;a href="https://www.npr.org/2026/10/12/nx-s1-5998976/pro-trump-ads-taxpayer-funds-federal-judge" target="_blank"&gt;nearly $22 million in taxpayer funds&lt;/a&gt; have been spent since the campaign began in late September. Almost $10 million of that was spent after Trump pledged on an Oct. 5 Truth Social post to fund the campaign privately. The White House has called the ads public service announcements, but a lawsuit by Common Cause and others argued they were funded without congressional approval, violating restrictions on taxpayer-funded publicity and propaganda.&lt;/p&gt;   &lt;div id="resg-s1-147809" class="bucketwrap image large"&gt;             &lt;div     class="imagewrap has-source-dimensions"     data-crop-type=""     style="         --source-width: 5097;         --source-height: 2867;     " &gt;         &lt;picture&gt;             &lt;source srcset="https://npr.brightspotcdn.com/dims3/default/strip/false/crop/5097x2867+0+265/resize/400/quality/85/format/webp/?url=http%3A%2F%2Fnpr-brightspot.s3.amazonaws.com%2F6f%2F5c%2F3f346e034949b36cd4c8b40fa6ce%2Fgettyimages-229945